  "issue_title": "[bug] OpenRouter client crashes (and drops cost accounting) on an HTTP-200 response with no completion",
  "issue_body": "**Describe the bug**\n\n`OpenRouterPool.chat._do` (`src/trinity/llm/openrouter_client.py`) parses the response body by blindly indexing `choices[0]` and `choice[\"message\"]`:\n\n```python\nresp.raise_for_status()\ndata = resp.json()\nchoice = data[\"choices\"][0]          # IndexError (empty) / KeyError (missing)\nusage = data.get(\"usage\", {})\npt = usage.get(\"prompt_tokens\", 0)\nct = usage.get(\"completion_tokens\", 0)\n_ledger_append(payload[\"model\"], pt, ct)\nreturn ChatResult(..., text=_message_text(choice[\"message\"]), ...)   # KeyError if no message\n```\n\nBut an OpenAI-compatible endpoint (OpenRouter especially) routinely returns **HTTP 200 with a body that carries no completion**:\n- content-moderation / safety block \u2192 `{\"choices\": [], \"usage\": {...}}`\n- an upstream-error envelope surfaced as 200 \u2192 `{\"error\": {...}}` (no `choices` key)\n- a choice with no `message` (reasoning/tool-only frames on some providers)\n\n`resp.raise_for_status()` passes (it's a 200), and the `IndexError`/`KeyError` is **not** one of the caught `httpx` transport types, so it propagates out of `_do` \u2192 out of the tenacity retry (`reraise=True`) \u2192 out of `chat()`. On the training path (`evaluate_candidate`'s `asyncio.gather(..., return_exceptions=True)`) the whole trajectory silently becomes reward 0.0; any caller without that guard aborts the run.\n\n**Two defects in one place:**\n1. **Crash / lost turn:** a valid 200-with-no-completion raises instead of degrading to an empty completion.\n2. **Cost under-reporting:** the crash happens *before* `_ledger_append`, so the prompt tokens of a moderated/empty \u2014 but still **billed** \u2014 call are never written to `TRINITY_COST_LEDGER`, and `scripts/cost_report.py` under-reports true spend.\n\n**Expected vs actual**\n\n- *Expected:* an empty/blocked 200 degrades to `ChatResult(text=\"\", finish_reason=\"error\")` with the `usage` tokens still recorded.\n- *Actual:* `IndexError`/`KeyError` propagates out of the retry and aborts the call (or silently zeros the trajectory); the billed tokens are dropped.\n\n**To reproduce**\n\n```python\nfrom trinity.llm.openrouter_client import _parse_completion  # after the fix\n# The response an OpenRouter moderation block returns as HTTP 200:\ndata = {\"id\": \"gen-x\", \"choices\": [], \"usage\": {\"prompt_tokens\": 812, \"completion_tokens\": 0}}\n# Before: data[\"choices\"][0] -> IndexError, straight out of chat().\n```\n\n**Environment**\n- Python version: 3.10+\n- GPU: not required (defect is in pure response parsing; reproducible with a response dict)\n- Commit hash: current `main` (`c23c767`)\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-11T04:16:05.000Z",
